Package: SimtablR
Title: Easy Publication-Ready Tables and Regression Analysis
Version: 3.1.1
Authors@R: person(given = "Matheus", family = "Trabuco Gonzalez", email
        = "matheustrabucogonzalez@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Streamlines the creation of descriptive frequency tables
        ('Table 1'), diagnostic test accuracy evaluations (sensitivity,
        specificity, predictive values), and multi-outcome regression
        summaries.  Features a grammar for publication-ready
        epidemiological tables built on design-aware effect measures,
        prevalence and odds ratio calculations, and seamless
        integration with 'flextable' for exporting results to
        'Microsoft Word' and 'PowerPoint'.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports: cli, digest, generics, rlang, sandwich, stats, tidyselect,
        utils
Suggests: dplyr, flextable, ggplot2, gt, haven, knitr, openxlsx,
        labelled, logistf, officer, pROC, rmarkdown, survival, EValue,
        testthat (>= 3.0.0), withr
VignetteBuilder: knitr
